cribe the bug**\n40\t\n41\t<!-- A clear and concise description of what the bug is. -->\n42\t\n43\t**To Reproduce**\n44\t\n45\t<!--\n46\tMinimal steps to reproduce the behavior with source code and Black's configuration.\n47\t-->\n48\t\n49\tFor example, take this code:\n50\t\n51\t```python\n52\tthis = \"code\"\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\tAnd run it with these arguments:\n56\t\n57\t```sh\n58\t$ black file.py --target-version py39\n59\t```\n60\t\n61\tThe resulting error is:\n62\t\n63\t> cannot format file.py: INTERNAL ERROR: ...\n64\t\n65\t**Expected behavior**\n66\t\n67\t<!-- A clear and concise description of what you expected to happen. -->\n68\t\n69\t**Environment**\n70\t\n71\t<!-- Pl\n72\t~~~~\n73\t\n74\t### candidate #5 (score 0.2, open, labels ['C: unstable formatting', 'F: fmtoff', 'T: bug'])\n75\ttitle: Unexpected error with Black 25.11.0 when fmt: off and fmt: on are used within block of comments\n76\t\n77\t~~~~ untrusted\n78\t<!--\n79\tPlease make sure that the bug is not already fixed either in newer versions or the\n80\tcurrent development version. To confirm this, you have three options:\n81\t\n82\t1. Update Black's version if a newer release exists: `pip install -U black`\n83\t2. Use the online formatter at <https://black.vercel.app/?version=main>, which will use\n84\t   the latest main branch.\n85\t3. Or run _Black_ on your machine:\n86\t   - create a new virtualenv (make sure it's the same Python version);\n87\t   - clone this repository;\n88\t   - run `pip install -e .[d]`;\n89\t   - run `pip install -r test_requirements.txt`\n90\t   - make sure it's sane by running `python -m pytest`; and\n91\t   - run `black` like you did last time.\n92\t-->\n93\t\n94\t**Describe the bug**\n95\t\n96\t<!-- A clear and concise description of what the bug is. -->\n97\t\n98\t**To Reproduce**\n99\t\n100\t<!--\n101\tMinimal steps to reproduce the behavior with source code and Black's configuration.\n102\t-->\n103\t\n104\tFor example, take this code:\n105\t\n106\t```python\n107\t