agent	Execute Claude Code CLI	2026-10-21T02:24:24.1975433Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEb4rNo9YCLqVWFxmcmk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S8YiYvYrxfDUuss6heLxah","name":"mcp__safeoutputs__add_comment","input":{"item_number":"8","body":"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\n\n**Reproduction:** Black 25.12.0 with `--target-version py313`: parse error (`Cannot parse for target version Python 3.13: 3:0: 2`). Reproduced with the snippet from the report.\n\n**Assessment:** The snippet is valid Python. A backslash continuation may place the next line at any column, and the line is then joined to the previous one. Black's parser should accept it, so this looks like a parser/tokenizer bug rather than invalid input or a style question. It appears when the continued line sits at column 0 inside an indented block.\n\n**Next step:** A maintainer should confirm. It would help to know whether older Black releases format this input and whether the error depends on the target version. I found no matching duplicate among the candidates.\n\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: none</sub>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":301,"cache_read_input_tokens":48303,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":301,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":32,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0511db67-9120-4a0c-bdf1-a11fe78f6e08","uuid":"417aa80c-3c3e-46a4-8302-ecd2fcaeb914","timestamp":"2026-10-21T02:24:24.194Z","request_id":"req_011CgEb4qzVGRcR9KUeZYCRi","tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01S8YiYvYrxfDUuss6heLxah","display_name":"Add Comment","server_display